ournald-cap.sh'","search_files infra/scripts '-cap.sh' returns FOUR scripts: docker-storage-cap.sh, journald-cap.sh, vartmp-cap.sh, container-cap.sh","compose-up.sh lines 99 & 113 install vartmp-cap.sh and container-cap.sh; observability.sh lines 1146 & 1240 consume them via --print-env","install-observability.sh lines 21-26: vartmp-cap.sh/container-cap.sh are DELIBERATELY handled differently (self-install a rebar-prefixed copy), so their manifest/exclusion disposition is a distinct decision"],"finding":"AC2's derivation rule `infra/**/*-cap.sh` will derive all four cap scripts (docker-storage-cap.sh, journald-cap.sh, vartmp-cap.sh, container-cap.sh), but AC1 and the whole plan address only two — leaving the gate red on vartmp-cap.sh and container-cap.sh with no disposition decided.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe33761d59e41e957","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1/AC2; 'What' section","norm_id":"nd096eddf0a4a7bba","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer adds the `infra/**/*-cap.sh` derivation; check_deploy_manifest.py now flags vartmp-cap.sh and container-cap.sh as UNCOVERED, and the plan gives no guidance on whether they go in a manifest or EXCLUSIONS"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementa