gree on detect-vs-apply.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.468,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Consequence: 'the new ceiling is not applied until some unrelated change happens to trigger the same action'","compose-up.sh lines 69-114 are the only callers of each `<cap>.sh --install` (the apply)","autodeploy.sh lines 246-260: MATERIALIZER_PATHS (which holds compose-up.sh) is DETECT-ONLY — the loop 'must NEVER re-run it', a change is 'signalled for a MANUAL operator apply, never auto-applied'","install-observability.sh lines 16-28: only copies docker-storage/journald to /usr/local/bin for the PROBE to READ, not to apply the ceiling"],"finding":"AC1 ('listed in the manifests whose actions actually consume them') combined with the Consequence framing ('the new ceiling is not applied') implies that listing the cap scripts causes the new ceiling to be applied, but the only action that APPLIES a cap is `<cap>.sh --install` via compose-up.sh, which is in the DETECT-ONLY MATERIALIZER_PATHS; the OBS_PATHS action only refreshes the probe's read-copy. Listing therefore restores a SIGNAL for a manual operator apply, not an auto-apply.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fab26d0947abf3011","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"'Consequence' section; Acceptance Criteria AC1","norm_id":"nc9177a6e6eda03ac","priority":0.132,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A cap-value-only commit: after the fix, autodeploy emits a detect signal (like config/edge paths) but still does NOT auto-apply the new daemon.json/journald/reaper ceiling — an operator must run compose-up.sh --install manually"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_f